{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I charged you at that time.</b> He is speaking with the children of Gad and the children of Reuben, and because they were included in all Israel he said אתכם, when he should have said אותם. And so we find at the end of the Torah (Deuteronomy 31:27): ״ויצו משה את הלוים לקוח את ספר התורה כי אנכי ידעתי את מריך״ — and this utterance was not to the Levites alone but to all Israel; rather, he spoke with them because the Levites were included."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:01.111720280Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}